# Status (2026-10-09): fixed the same day (IO may be listed; a `*rest` branch gets its arguments packed).
# Bug: `in IO` works (fixed 2026-10-04), but IO cannot be listed in the type-list form `(A|B).f(x)`:
#   error: `IO` is not a type; `(...)` lists types (Struct types or built-in types)
# Workaround in ruby_progressbar.sake and highline.sake: a case/in with one branch per stream type.
require "stringio"
def emit(o, s) = (IO|StringIO).print(o, s)
emit(IO.stdout, "to stdout\n")
sio = StringIO.new
emit(sio, "to a StringIO")
p(StringIO.string(sio))
